e outline: the north gallery range (8.5 m) with north-lit clerestory monitors over the galleries and windows on its north front, the Asian Art Wing taken as its north-west part, the entrance rotunda at the point under its tetrahedral skylight peaking 60 ft (18.3 m) up, the east wing running south to the tall gateway and its forecourt, the west wing and a cross range closing the court, the court laid out as a water garden with stones; pale rendered walls, white parapets and roofs; the drive on the east and campus oaks and pines. Still guessed: which part of the outline is which addition, every height, the clerestories, the gateway's form, the court's planting."}